                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="496621" author="JIRAUSER19573" created="Mon, 22 Jun 2026 22:09:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&#160;The issue for OST_WRITE described in &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15863&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;LU-15863&lt;/a&gt;is already taken care of by this below patch -&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/45459&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/45459&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But this fix looks like wouldn&apos;t cover the race for OST_SETATTR.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ofd_setattr_hdl() {
....
....
 &#160; &#160;fo = ofd_object_find_exists(tsi-&amp;gt;tsi_env, ofd, &amp;amp;tsi-&amp;gt;tsi_fid);
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (IS_ERR(fo))
	GOTO(out, rc = PTR_ERR(fo));

 &#160;  la_from_obdo(&amp;amp;fti-&amp;gt;fti_attr, &amp;amp;body-&amp;gt;oa, body-&amp;gt;oa.o_valid);
&#160; &#160; fti-&amp;gt;fti_attr.la_valid &amp;amp;= ~LA_TYPE;&#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* setting objects attributes (including owner/group) */&lt;/span&gt;

&#160; &#160; rc = ofd_attr_set(tsi-&amp;gt;tsi_env, fo, &amp;amp;fti-&amp;gt;fti_attr, &amp;amp;body-&amp;gt;oa);
&#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (rc != 0)
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; GOTO(out_put, rc);
...
....
}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In OST_SETATTR case, if the object is missing during replay, it can return &lt;tt&gt;-ENOENT&lt;/tt&gt; before &lt;tt&gt;ofd_attr_set()&lt;/tt&gt; is ever called. And there is no guarantee that this request will first go through the LVB init path that has the &lt;tt&gt;EINPROGRESS&lt;/tt&gt; retry logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OST_SETATTR &lt;b&gt;doesn&apos;t&lt;/b&gt; have an explicit recreate/retry logic like ofd_prepwr_write() that forces the write replay and thus leverages the fix through ofd_lvb change in the above patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496675" author="gerrit" created="Tue, 23 Jun 2026 21:25:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Sonia Sharma &amp;lt;sonia.sh.sharma@oracle.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66826&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66826&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
